This C program fulfills the user's request by reading current from an MLX91219 Hall-effect current sensor using an ADS1115 analog-to-digital converter on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the `pigpio` library for I2C communication and handles errors gracefully. The program configures the ADS1115 for single-shot mode, a gain of ±4.096V, and a sampling rate of 128 samples per second. It reads the current every 500ms and logs it to the console, converting the raw ADC value to amperes based on the MLX91219's sensitivity and zero-current offset. On receiving a SIGINT signal, it cleans up resources and terminates the GPIO before exiting.

