This C program fulfills the user's request by reading temperature and pressure data from a TDK ICP-10125 sensor connected to the Raspberry Pi Zero W's I2C bus 1 at address 0x67. It logs the timestamped readings to a CSV file named `environmental_data.csv` and displays the data in real-time on the console. The program uses the `libgpiod` library for I2C operations and handles errors and resource release meticulously. It includes signal handling for graceful shutdown upon receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM signals. The raw ADC values are converted to temperature in °C and pressure in Pa using the official calibration formulas provided by the sensor's datasheet. The program samples data every 5 seconds and retries after a 5-second delay if an error occurs during I2C operations.

