This C program reads analog values from a soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It configures SPI in mode 0 (CPOL=0, CPHA=0), at a clock speed of 1 MHz, and reads from channel 0 every 5 seconds. The moisture percentage is calculated and clamped to the 0-100 range before being printed to the console. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing the SPI device and exiting gracefully.

