This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi GPIO and SPI interfaces. It reads moisture levels from a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI and controls a water pump based on the moisture readings. The program logs every moisture reading and pump state change to a circular buffer, prints the buffer after each sample, and handles errors gracefully. It also demonstrates basic signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM, though in this example, the signals are ignored (`SIG_IGN`). 

