This C program uses the `pigpio` library to control a water pump connected to GPIO18 and reads a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. It maps the ADC values to a moisture percentage, logs events, and controls the pump based on moisture thresholds. The program gracefully handles SPI errors with retries and cleans up resources on exit or when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM signals.

