This C program reads three Texas Instruments DRV5055VA Hall-Effect sensors connected to GPIO4, GPIO17, and GPIO27 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+, using the libgpiod API. It simulates the analog-to-digital conversion by interpreting the digital logic state of each GPIO pin as the sensor output. The magnetic field strength is calculated and logged to a file named `magnetic_log.txt` in comma-separated format. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown and includes robust error handling for GPIO access and file I/O.

