This C program uses the `pigpio` library to control GPIO pins and the SPI interface on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads an analog value from a Keyes KY-038 sound sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI, with the MCP3008's chip select pin connected to GPIO8. If the sound level exceeds a threshold of 500 (10-bit ADC value), it turns on an LED connected to GPIO16 and logs the timestamp to "sound_events.log". The LED stays on for 500 ms after the sound level exceeds the threshold. The program debounces the sound level trigger and handles SPI transfer failures, invalid ADC channel selection, and GPIO initialization errors gracefully. Upon receiving a SIGINT signal, it cleans up resources and exits cleanly.

