This C program reads the distance from a Sharp GP2Y0A21YK0F IR distance sensor connected to GPIO 17 on a Raspberry Pi 5. It treats the GPIO input as a digital signal (0V or 3.3V) and converts this to a distance using a simple linear formula. The program logs each reading with a timestamp to "distance_log.txt" and activates a pet feeder if the computed distance is below 200 mm. It handles errors gracefully by retrying after 1 second if an operation fails. On receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM, it unexports the GPIO and exits cleanly.

