This C program fulfills the user's request by monitoring soil moisture using a DFRobot resistive soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC over SPI channel 0 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the pigpio library for GPIO control and the SPI interface for ADC operations. The program initializes pigpio, sets up SPI with proper configuration, reads ADC values every 60 seconds, logs readings with timestamps, handles errors, and cleans up resources on exit or when interrupted by a SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

