This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi GPIO and SPI interfaces. It reads the moisture level from a YL-69 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI channel 0. The moisture level is converted to a percentage and logged to a CSV file every 60 seconds. The program handles errors gracefully and releases resources on all exit paths. The `signal_handler` function ensures that the program terminates cleanly upon receiving a SIGINT signal.

