This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It implements a basic parking-assist system using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and an SG90 servo. The program initializes `pigpio`, configures GPIO pins, measures distances, maps distances to servo angles, logs data, and handles signal interruptions for graceful shutdown. It ensures proper resource management and error handling throughout its execution.

