This C program initializes the pigpio library, sets up I2C communication with the VL53L1X sensor, verifies the sensor model ID, performs a software reset, configures the timing budget, starts ranging, and reads distance measurements every 50 ms. It also handles errors at each step and cleans up resources on SIGINT. The distance readings are logged to a POSIX message queue named "distance_queue". If the measured distance falls below 100mm, a buzzer connected to GPIO23 is activated.

