This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with a Raspberry Pi GPIO pins and an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor for distance measurement, as well as an SG90 micro servo for visual feedback. It initializes `pigpio`, measures the distance, calculates the corresponding servo angle, and sets the servo position. The program handles initialization errors, sensor timeouts, and gracefully stops the servo and cleans up resources on receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

