This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with a Sensirion SCD40 CO2 sensor over I2C on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It initializes pigpio, sets up I2C communication, sends commands to the sensor, reads data, verifies the CRC, logs the air quality data to a file, and handles cleanup and SIGINT signals. The program ensures proper error handling and resource release at all stages.

