This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with a Texas Instruments TMP102 temperature sensor connected to a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B via I2C. It reads the temperature every 5 seconds, converts the raw reading to degrees Celsius, and logs it to a CSV file named `temperature_log.csv`. The program handles errors gracefully and terminates cleanly upon receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C). It includes necessary error checking and resource management to ensure robust operation.

