This C program uses the `pigpio` library to control a PWM-driven cooling fan connected to GPIO18 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the CPU temperature from `/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp` and adjusts the fan speed based on a linear mapping from 40°C to 70°C. The duty cycle is logged every 5 seconds along with the timestamp and temperature to `fan_log.txt`. The program handles initialization errors, file write errors, and gracefully exits on receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM signals, stopping the fan and cleaning up resources.

