This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 5. It sets up GPIO 17 as an input to read from the MAX9814 microphone amplifier and GPIO 18 as an output to control the gain. The program continuously polls GPIO 17 for rising edges (indicating sound peaks) and logs these events to `audio_log.txt` with timestamps. It handles initialization errors, GPIO setup errors, and cleanup on exit or when interrupted by a signal (SIGINT or SIGTERM).

