This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It monitors two DRV5032FJDBZR Hall-Effect sensors connected to GPIO 17 and GPIO 18 to measure the RPM of a rotating shaft. The program implements a debounce mechanism with a delay of approximately 5 ms to avoid false readings. It calculates the RPM based on the assumption of 2 pulses per revolution and prints the RPM to the console. Additionally, it logs sensor state changes to a CSV file named `shaft_log.txt` with timestamps.

The program handles potential initialization errors for both `pigpio` and GPIO operations, as well as file I/O errors when opening the log file. It ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including handling the SIGINT signal (Ctrl+C) by closing resources and exiting the program.

