This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 5 for obstacle detection and LED control. It initializes GPIO pins for four infrared sensors and an LED, reads sensor data in a loop, and controls the LED based on the sensor input. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by cleaning up resources and exiting gracefully. It uses non-blocking `usleep` for polling the sensors every 50 ms to avoid blocking signal handling.

