This C program reads ambient light from a BH1750 I2C sensor at address 0x23 and adjusts the brightness of an APA102 LED strip via SPI. It uses direct I2C and SPI access through `/dev/i2c-1` and `/dev/spidev0.0` respectively. The BH1750 is initialized in One-Time High-Resolution mode, and the lux value is converted from the raw data using a conversion factor. The brightness of the APA102 LED strip is adjusted proportionally to the measured lux, mapping the lux range [10, 300] to the APA102's 5-bit global brightness [0, 31]. The program handles SIGINT by turning off the LEDs and closing all file descriptors. Error handling is implemented for I/O operations and bus errors.

