This C program initializes a GY-50 L3G4200D gyroscope connected to the Raspberry Pi Zero W via I2C bus 1. It reads the gyroscope data, calibrates the zero-rate offsets, and logs the readings to a file. It also handles potential errors and resource cleanup on exit. The program runs in an infinite loop, reading the gyroscope at 50 ms intervals and writing the data to a log file. If any axis exceeds 50 dps, it prints a warning and logs the alert. The program gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing resources and exiting.

