This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interface with an Analog Devices ADIS16448 IMU connected via SPI on Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It initializes the SPI and GPIO correctly, handles errors, and cleans up resources on exit. The program reads gyroscope and accelerometer data from the specified registers, scales the values according to the provided factors, and prints them every 100 ms. It also handles Ctrl+C interruptions gracefully by closing the SPI connection and terminating the pigpio instance.

