This C program initializes the Adafruit LIS3MDL Triple-Axis Magnetometer on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ over I2C, configures it for continuous conversion mode at 80 Hz ODR with high-performance mode enabled, reads the magnetic field data, applies calibration constants, and writes the X, Y, Z values to a log file (`magnetic_log.txt`) at 10 Hz. It also includes a simple metal detector alert mechanism that prints to stderr when the total magnetic field magnitude exceeds 800 mG. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing the I2C file descriptor and the log file cleanly. It retries initialization up to 3 times if an error occurs during the initialization process.

