This C program initializes the pigpio library, opens the I2C bus, verifies the presence of the STMicroelectronics LSM6DSR accelerometer and gyroscope, configures the sensor registers for desired ranges and rates, and then enters a loop where it reads sensor data every 100 ms. It handles errors at every step, including initialization failures, I2C bus errors, register write failures, and short or failed burst reads. The program also installs a SIGINT handler to gracefully exit and clean up resources when interrupted with Ctrl+C.

