This C program reads the active-high digital output of an SW-420 vibration sensor connected to GPIO17 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the libgpiod API. It polls for both rising and falling edges with a timeout specified by a command-line argument (defaulting to 1000 ms if not provided). It logs each edge event to `vibration_events.log` with an ISO-8601 timestamp and checks for a simulated earthquake alert condition based on a sliding window of the last 5 events. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to exit gracefully, releasing resources and closing the log file. It also checks every libgpiod call and syscall for errors, printing diagnostics to stderr.

