This C program uses the libgpiod library to control four 5V relay modules on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It initializes the GPIO pins as outputs with active-low semantics, sets them to HIGH (inactive) at startup, and then activates each relay sequentially for 5 seconds every 24 hours. The start time of each watering cycle is logged to a file named `watering_log.txt`. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by releasing all GPIO lines, closing the chip, and exiting cleanly. 

To compile the program, use the command:

```bash
gcc -o watering watering.c -lgpiod
```

Ensure that the libgpiod library is installed on your system before compiling. This program assumes that the GPIO pins are correctly wired to the relay modules and that the Raspberry Pi is configured to allow access to the GPIO pins.

