This C program fulfills the user's request by reading angular velocity data from an InvenSense MPU-6050 gyroscope connected via SPI to a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It uses libgpiod for GPIO control and spidev for SPI communication. The program initializes SPI and GPIO, sets up the gyroscope communication, reads data from the gyroscope, checks for exceeding angular velocity thresholds, and blinks an LED when thresholds are exceeded. It stores the readings in a circular buffer and prints the buffer upon receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C). The program cleans up resources on exit and handles errors gracefully.

