This C program uses the `pigpio` library to initialize and manage GPIO and SPI operations on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It reads angular rate data from an Analog Devices ADXRS290 gyroscope connected via SPI on channel 0, with a clock speed of 1 MHz and SPI mode 0. The program samples both X and Y axis data at approximately 100 Hz, converting the raw data from 16-bit two's complement to degrees per second using the provided sensitivity factor. It logs the data to a file named `gyro_data.csv`, appending new samples with a timestamp and the raw rate values.

The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by gracefully closing the SPI connection, flushing and closing the file, and terminating `pigpio`, ensuring all resources are released. It attempts to reinitialize SPI up to three times if a read fails, before exiting with an error message.

Please ensure you have the `pigpio` library installed and properly set up on your Raspberry Pi before compiling and running this program. The `pigpio` library can be installed via `sudo apt-get install pigpio` on Debian-based systems.

