This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi GPIO pins and perform ultrasonic distance measurements with an HC-SR04 sensor. It handles GPIO pin setup, interrupt callbacks for detecting the echo pulse, and logging valid distance measurements with timestamps to a CSV file. The program also includes error handling for various scenarios and gracefully handles SIGINT signals to terminate the measurement loop. The mutex ensures safe access to shared variables that are updated from interrupt context.

