This C program uses the libgpiod library to control a Parker Hannifin Series 9 General Purpose Miniature Solenoid Valve connected to GPIO18 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the watering duration from a configuration file named `watering.conf`, which must contain a single line in the format `duration=<seconds>`, where `<seconds>` is a positive integer between 1 and 3600. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by setting a flag, which is checked in the main loop to shut down the valve early if necessary. On all exit paths, it releases the GPIO line and closes the chip to ensure the valve is left off. Error checking is performed for every libgpiod call, and descriptive error messages are printed to stderr. Status messages are printed to stdout for each valve on/off transition and the configured duration.

