This C program fulfills the user's request by interfacing with an Omron D7S seismic sensor over I2C on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It reads tri-axial acceleration data, converts it to g-force units, and logs the data to a CSV file (`seismic_data.csv`) with timestamps. The program supports command-line options for changing the I2C address, interval between readings, and output file name. It handles transient I2C read/write errors with retries and logs all errors to a separate file (`seismic_error.log`). The program gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing resources and exiting cleanly.

