This C program uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the states of a Keywish 3-Way Tracking Sensor connected to GPIO4, GPIO17, and GPIO27, each configured as an input with pull-up resistors enabled. The program runs a main loop at 10 Hz (100 ms period) and logs sensor states to the console. If all three sensors detect an obstacle simultaneously, it sends an emergency stop message over the serial port `/dev/ttyAMA0` at 115200 baud, 8N1, without flow control. The program handles initialization errors, GPIO setup errors, sensor reading errors, and serial port errors gracefully, ensuring resources are released properly on all exit paths.
